# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and checked out as LF.
#
# Without this, a file committed with CRLF is rewritten IN FULL the next time
# anyone runs `npm run format` — prettier normalizes to LF, both by its own
# default and because `.editorconfig` declares `end_of_line = lf`. The diff is
# the whole file rather than the change, so it lands as unrelated churn inside
# whatever PR happens to be open. Balor hit exactly that in WP3, which is where
# this came from. Copied from hyb-electron-template (HTOO-236).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so git never tries to translate them and never offers them
# as a text diff. The list states the format; git's own guess reads only the
# first 8000 bytes for a NUL. Corvath tracks png, webp and jpg today (the
# icons, the deck art under bundled/ and the renderer assets).
*.png binary
*.bmp binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
# A deck export is a zip (deckPackage.ts). None is tracked today; a test
# fixture that adds one must not be normalized.
*.corvathdeck binary

# Generated. Marking it linguist-generated keeps it out of PR diffs by default;
# the lockfile is still tracked and still reviewed when it actually matters.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
